---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../config/site';
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Construction & Estimating Disclaimer"
  metaTitle={`Construction & Cost Estimating Disclaimer | ${siteConfig.name}`}
  metaDescription={`Important disclaimer regarding material quantity takeoffs, building codes, structural engineering, and regional cost ranges on ${siteConfig.name}.`}
  pathname="/disclaimer/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Disclaimer', href: '/disclaimer/' }]}
>
  <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border border-amber-300 dark:border-amber-800 text-amber-950 dark:text-amber-200 font-medium text-sm sm:text-base">
    Estimates generated by {siteConfig.name} are for planning and educational purposes only. Always verify field measurements, product coverage labels, local building codes, and structural requirements with a licensed professional before purchasing materials or beginning construction.
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-6">
    1. Material Quantities &amp; Substrate Variability
  </h2>
  <p>
    Actual material consumption depends on surface porosity, subfloor flatness, excavation grading accuracy, mortar joint tooling, wood moisture content, and installer technique. Before cutting materials or ordering non-returnable custom batches, confirm your measurements on site and check the manufacturer's printed technical data sheet (TDS).
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-6">
    2. Building Codes &amp; Underground Utilities (Call 811)
  </h2>
  <p>
    Before digging post holes, footings, or trenches, always call <strong>811</strong> (or visit <a href="https://call811.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blueprint underline">call811.com</a>) at least 2–3 business days in advance to have underground utility lines marked for free. Structural elements such as deck ledgers, stair stringers, retaining walls over 4 feet, and load-bearing footings require municipal permits and adherence to local amendments of the International Residential Code (IRC).
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-6">
    3. Regional Cost Ranges
  </h2>
  <p>
    Our state and national cost guides reflect typical residential remodeling ranges and BLS occupational wage data. Actual contractor quotes will vary based on site accessibility, demolition complexity, hazardous material remediation (e.g., lead paint or asbestos prior to 1978), and seasonal labor demand.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
